-- v0.1.5_kernel.sql: the 0.1.4 -> 0.1.5 gap. Idempotent: every statement is guarded, every row by key.
-- Adds (kernel-owned): the library contract family beside etg.contracts_db_* and etg.contracts_modules_*: the third-party
-- libraries the application depends on (contracts_primitives_libraries, the exact pin, a dev filter, the advisory reference),
-- one hash row per published artifact (contracts_primitives_libraries_hashes), and the models, model fields and functions we
-- call on them (contracts_primitives_libraries_models / _models_fields / _functions; a function's input model is its parameters,
-- its output model its return, 'void' the empty model). Hand-authored, never reflected: populate gains no pass, and only what is
-- called is declared, so a version bump forces the signatures and models to be re-verified. Scope: every caller that runs in the
-- requirements.txt environment, i.e. the application (main.py, server/) and its REPL tooling (scripts/scriptlib.py, repl.py).
-- The rows are kernel package data ('make requirements' emits requirements.txt / requirements-dev.txt from them); the first
-- rows ship here.
-- Moves the database version to 0.1.5.
SET ANSI_NULLS ON;
GO
SET QUOTED_IDENTIFIER ON;
GO

